` THE FISH EFFECT. every fish on the board is drawn with it. it tilts the fish like a card in 3d,
` and it draws more copies of the fish stacked up behind. the routine that feeds it, frame_fish_fx, is in fish_routines.
global FISH_FX_ID = 2
global FISH_STACK_EASE# = .2 `how much of the way a stack moves toward its real count on a frame

` LIVE MOVES. a swap, or the cursor moving on its own, does not stop the game while it plays out. it gets
` started, and then it gets moved along a little on every frame until it is done. that is what lets the
` player keep moving and swapping while a combo is popping, falling, and filling back in.
` only one plays at a time, and the rest wait in the queue of moves. the special moves still stop the
` game while they play, so they wait for the board to settle first.
` a swap cannot touch a fish that the combo is busy with: one that is popping, one that is falling, or a
` new one that is dropping in. isCellLocked says which those are. the places that they are leaving or
` heading for are empty, so there is nothing to swap with there either.
` startLiveMove and stepLiveMove, in fish_funcs, do the work. process_input and frame_combo_input, in
` fish_routines_input, call them.
global LIVE_MOVE_ACTIVE = 0 `1 while one is playing out
global LIVE_MOVE_IS_SWAP = 0 `1 if it swaps two fish, and 0 if only the cursor moves
global LIVE_MOVE_A = 0 `the cell that it started on
global LIVE_MOVE_B = 0 `and the cell that it is headed for
global LIVE_MOVE_FROM_X = 0
global LIVE_MOVE_FROM_Y = 0
global LIVE_MOVE_TO_X = 0
global LIVE_MOVE_TO_Y = 0
global LIVE_MOVE_DIR_X = 0
global LIVE_MOVE_DIR_Y = 0
global LIVE_MOVE_FREE = 0 `1 if it is the swap of the "free move" card, which is not counted as a move
global LIVE_MOVE_HOLD = 0 `1 when no new one may start, because a part of a combo is done and waiting to move on
global COMBO_PHASE = 0 `what a combo is doing right now. 0 is nothing, 1 is popping, 2 is falling, and 3 is filling back in.

` a move that cannot be made gives the cursor a quick shake, toward the way that it was asked to go and
` back, so that the press does not look like it was missed. stepCursorShake, in fish_funcs, plays it.
global CURSOR_SHAKE_TWEEN_ID
global CURSOR_SHAKING = 0
global CURSOR_SHAKE_DIR_X = 0
global CURSOR_SHAKE_DIR_Y = 0
global CURSOR_SHAKE_SIZE = 4 `how far it goes, in pixels
global CURSOR_SHAKE_TIME = 220 `how long it lasts, in milliseconds

` STACKS. a cell can hold more fish, stacked up behind the one that shows. the stack goes wherever the fish
` goes, and every fish in it scores when it pops. cards are the only way to get one.
` with "bottom feeder", a fish that lands on the bottom row, from a row above it, has a chance to pick up
` one more. fishHitBottom, in fish_funcs, is where that happens.
` with "contagious smile", a fish that is right next to a fish that pops has a chance to. handle_combos does that.
` when a stacked fish pops, the fish in its stack pop first, one at a time, and each one scores. the one in
` front goes last.
global FISH_STACK_MAX = 3 `the most fish that can be stacked up behind one. the fish effect cannot draw more.
global FISH_STACK_POP_GAP = 380`how many milliseconds there are between one fish of a stack popping and the next
global BOTTOM_FEEDER_CHANCE = 30 `how many landings in a hundred pick up a fish
global BOTTOM_FEEDER_CHANCE_2 = 60 `and how many do with the second copy of the card
global CONTAGIOUS_SMILE_CHANCE = 10 `how many fish in a hundred pick one up from a pop next to them, for every time the card has been taken
global CONTAGIOUS_SMILE_MAX = 4 `how many times the card can be taken

` BOTTOMS UP. with the "bottoms up" card, every move has a chance to turn one fish on the board belly up.
` the fish rolls over, top over bottom, and stays that way wherever it goes, the same as a stack does.
` when the cursor comes to a fish that is belly up, that fish pops, and so does every belly up fish
` right next to it. they pop as a group of their own, however few of them there are.
` rollBellyUpFish and popBellyUpFish, in fish_funcs, do those, and frame_fish_fx draws the fish turned over.
global BOTTOMS_UP_CHANCE = 10 `how many moves in a hundred turn a fish over, for every time the card has been taken
global BOTTOMS_UP_MAX = 3 `how many times the card can be taken
global BELLY_UP_ROLL_DUE = 0 `1 when a move has been made, and the board has not settled since
global BELLY_UP_EASE# = .2 `how much of the way a fish rolls toward where it should be on a frame
global BELLY_UP_ROCK# = .3 `how far a belly up fish rocks from side to side as it floats, in radians

` SHOCKWAVES. a move or a combo sends a ring out across the board, and the fish ride it as it passes under them,
` like things floating on a ripple. the ring is a bump in the water. a fish on top of the bump lifts up, so it
` gets bigger. a fish on the front of the bump gets pushed away from where the ring started, and
` leans away from it, and a fish on the back of the bump gets pulled back, and leans back.
` the rings add up. where two of them cross, a fish gets the lift of both, and the pushes of both.
` spawnShockwave and spawnShockwaveToward, in fish_funcs, start one, and frame_fish_fx turns them into what the fish do.
global SHOCK_COUNT = 24 `how many can be going at once. past that, a new one takes the place of the oldest.
global dim SHOCKS(SHOCK_COUNT) as shockwave
global dim SHOCK_LIVE(SHOCK_COUNT) `which of them are going on this frame
global SHOCK_LIVE_COUNT = 0
global SHOCK_SPEED# = 4.5 `how fast the ring grows, in cells per second
global SHOCK_WIDTH# = 2.5 `how thick the ring is, in cells, from the middle of it to either edge. a thick one rolls over a fish slowly.
global SHOCK_LIFE = 2000 `how many milliseconds one lasts. it gets weaker the whole time.
global SHOCK_ATTACK = 160 `how many milliseconds one takes to swell up at the start, so that it does not pop in

` how strong a ring is, where 1 does all of the things below in full. only the big things get a strong one.
` the cursor moving on its own does not send one out at all.
global SHOCK_SWAP_STRENGTH# = .2 `for a swap
global SHOCK_ABILITY_STRENGTH# = 1 `for a special move, like the bomb
global SHOCK_COMBO_STRENGTH# = .25 `for the smallest group of fish that can pop
global SHOCK_COMBO_GROW# = .25 `and how much stronger it gets for every fish past that, up to 1

` what a ring of strength 1 does to a fish.
` the fish are pixel art, drawn at one pixel of the picture to one pixel of the world, so making one bigger
` or leaning it makes some of its pixels double up and some drop out. the push lands on whole pixels to stay crisp.
global SHOCK_LIFT# = .4 `how much bigger the fish gets on top of the bump. 1 is twice as big.
global SHOCK_TILT# = .9 `how far it leans on the side of the bump, in radians
global SHOCK_PUSH# = .3 `how far it gets pushed on the side of the bump, where 1 is the size of a fish
global SHOCK_BOB# = 0 `how far it floats up the screen on top of the bump, the same way. this is off.

` rings that pile up cannot add up forever. the sum bends over as it gets close to these, instead
` of stopping dead at them, so a second ring always shows on top of a first.
global SHOCK_LIFT_MAX# = 1.6 `the most lift, where 1 is what one ring of strength 1 does
global SHOCK_LEAN_MAX# = 1.5 `and the most push and lean. the effect falls apart close to edge on, so this times SHOCK_TILT has to stay under 1.57.

