` THE SCORE THAT SHOWS. a combo is scored all at once, when it is found, but its fish pop one after another.
` so the bar of the round's progress does not show CURRENT_SCORE. it shows SCORE_SHOWN, which gets the points
` of each fish at the moment that the fish pops, and catches up with CURRENT_SCORE by the time the last one has.
` the round is over when the score that shows gets to the end of the bar, so that the bar is seen filling up first.
` queueScore and stepScoreTicks, in fish_funcs, do the work.
global SCORE_SHOWN = 0

` when the bar fills up, the round is over. the upgrade screen does not come up right away, though. it waits
` for the board to settle, so that fish which are still popping get to finish. the bar stays full that whole
` time, and it fizzes with bubbles to show that an upgrade is on its way.
` the bar stays full while the upgrade screen is up, too. only once an upgrade has been picked does the bar
` empty out and start on the next round. advanceScoreBar, in fish_funcs, does that.
` a big combo can score far past the end of the bar. the score is kept, but the next round never starts
` more than SCORE_CARRY_MAX# of the way along, so one combo cannot win two rounds in a row.
global SCORE_BAR_HOLD = 0 `0 is not full. 1 is full, and waiting for the board to settle. 2 is full, with the upgrade screen asked for.
global SCORE_CARRY_MAX# = .5 `how much of the next round's bar the points scored past the end can fill, at the most
global SCORE_BAR_FIZZ_MS = 0 `when the full bar lets off its next bubbles
global SCORE_BAR_FIZZ_GAP = 55 `how many milliseconds there are between them

` the bar shakes a little while it is filling up, and it shakes more, and is brighter, while it is full and fizzing
global SCORE_BAR_LAST_FILL# = 0 `how full the bar was drawn on the last frame, to tell when it is filling up
global SCORE_TICK_MAX = 600 `more than every fish on the biggest board, with a full stack behind each one
global SCORE_TICK_COUNT = 0 `how many are waiting
global dim SCORE_TICK_MS(SCORE_TICK_MAX) `when each one is due
global dim SCORE_TICK_POINTS(SCORE_TICK_MAX) `and how many points it is worth

` THE MULTIPLIER. every fish that pops scores this many times what it would have.
` a swap that makes something pop fills the multiplier's bar a little. when the bar is full, the multiplier
` goes up by one, and the bar starts again from empty. a swap that pops nothing empties the bar, and takes
` one off of the multiplier, down to 1 at the least.
` the bar takes 3 more swaps in a row to fill every time: 2 to get to x2, 5 to get to x3, 8 to get to x4.
` how many it takes follows from the multiplier, so when the multiplier goes down, so does how many it takes.
` there is no top to the multiplier. the higher it is, the longer the next one takes, and the more every pop is worth.
` only swaps count. the special moves, and the cursor moving on its own, do not fill the bar or empty it.
` the routines are in fish_routines_multiplier.
global SCORE_MULTIPLIER = 1
global MULT_FIRST_REQUIRED = 2 `how many swaps in a row it takes to get from x1 to x2
global MULT_REQUIRED_STEP = 3 `and how many more it takes for every multiplier after that
global MULT_PROGRESS = 0 `how many swaps in a row have popped something, since the bar was last empty
global MULT_PENDING_SWAPS = 0 `swaps that have been made, that handle_combos has not looked at the board since
global MULT_POS as vec = {
    x = 32,
    y = 70
}
global MULT_BAR_WIDTH = 64
global MULT_BAR_BACK_SPRITE
global MULT_BAR_FILL_SPRITE
global MULT_TEXT_ID
global MULT_NUM_TEXT_ID
global MULT_FILL_TWEEN_ID
global MULT_PUNCH_TWEEN_ID `1 when the multiplier has just changed, dying away to 0
global MULT_PUNCH_DIR = 0 `1 if it went up, and -1 if it went down

